G03.approach:
The gap is real and fixable as a single-pass correctness fix with no caps change. Four findings from the spec and the code change its shape.
(1) It is worse than the gap says for the TMUs. SPEC §8.21 L2836: a TMU's other/local/mselect_7 inputs ALWAYS come from combineMode, whatever bit 31 says. So any leftover TMU combineMode silently rewires the HAL's legacy TM_TC_REPLACE/MULT/ADD (vcr_3dregs.h:164-175). On .124 our MesaFX programs its combines through Glide's COMBINE extension (diget.c NAPALM_EXT_STR; fxapi.c:575; fxsetup.h:574-700, 828-838). A clean Glide close clears only combineMode bit 29 (gsst.c:3295-3303). So after ANY OpenGL title, D3D draws through MesaFX's last extended combine on the FBI (bit 31: the muxes come from combineMode, L2826-2834) and on both TMUs.
(2) The listed fix would arm a trap. TMU texture chroma substitution switches on when chromaRange[30:29]=3 and combineMode[30]=0 (L2825, L3534). Glide parks a TMU constant colour in the chroma registers while bit 30 is set (gtex.c:1931; distate.c:1656-1666). Zeroing combineMode alone re-arms substitution, so TMU chromaRange must be zeroed first.
(3) Clip rect 1, stipple and FBI chroma are NOT live hazards today. Clip1 needs clipLeftRight1[31] or renderMode[21]; Glide never sets bit 31 (gglide.c:3349-3357), and the HAL writes renderMode in full with bit 21 = 0. Stipple and FBI chroma need fbzMode[2]/[1], which compute_regs never sets (vcrdd_d3d.c:978-986). They are written or pinned for later gaps only.
(4) Correction to hal-02. combineMode, sliCtrl, aaCtrl, chipMask, chromaKey and chromaRange are WRITE-ONLY (SPEC L2316-2347; reads 'undefined', L2225). The 11-12 dump reading 0 acquits nothing.
FIX (Diag\D3DSafe bit 1). New Win32-free vcr_3d_d3d_baseline_seq(napalm, w) in vcr_3dseq.h, 22 writes on a VSA-100 (0 on Banshee/Voodoo3), in this order:
- chipMask=0xFFFFFFFF (first: chip 0 must take what follows);
- sliCtrl=0 (directly behind it, as Reset3D);
- 12 x nopCMD at chip field TMU0|TMU1 (offset 0x1800+0x120: the spec's 2PPC exit, L2840; the same field vcrdd_3d.c:111 already writes on silicon);
- TMU chromaRange=0 (0x1800+0x138);
- combineMode=0 (broadcast: FBI+TMU0+TMU1);
- aaCtrl=0 (its offsets act even with AA off, L3442; bit 31 must be 0 with setup-unit culling);
- stencilMode=0 and stencilOp=0 at every depth (as the vendor, D6DP2.C:5459-5469/6107-6129);
- FBI chromaRange=0;
- clipLeftRight1=0 and clipBottomTop1=0.
Never renderMode, buffers, the clip, fbz/alpha/fog/texture registers, or a non-zero sliCtrl.
