G17.gating:
The format goes behind Diag\D3DBigTex bit 3 (value 8), a positive flag, default OFF (absent = off).
- It is read once at boot, like bits 0-2, and is honoured only with bit 2 (A8R8G8B8): pd->tex_x8 = tex_32 && VCR_INFO_F_TEXX8.
- .124's armed value goes from 7 to 15.
- The NewDark launcher's (v & 5) == 5 test already treats 0xf as armed, so it is unaffected.

What happens with the switch off:
- no D3DBigTex: the default 3-entry list, and tex_view never sets alpha_one;
- D3DBigTex=7 (.124 today): the 9-entry list and every register byte-for-byte unchanged, since no X8 surface can exist;
- bit 3 without bit 2: unchanged.

It is NOT safe to land default-on. Offering a format changes what every D3D title may pick (UE2, NewDark, Max Payne and DX6 enumerators). It must be proven in one supervised clean boot where bit 3 is the only change; it then joins the D3DBigTex default-on decision (G20).

Safe to land default-on now:
- the untextured-draw counters (log only, no register change);
- the vcr_texfmt.h move, as long as the native test pins today's lists and registers;
- the new d3dprobe tests (explicit-only; they SKIP, or FAIL when named, where X8 is not offered).

