G48.gating:
Default OFF behind Diag\D3DFastSetup bit 1 (0x02), using perf.md P3's switch and its bit order:
- bit 0: packed colour, reserved for G58;
- bit 1: FIFO credit (this item);
- bits 2-3: strip/fan continuation and autostrip, reserved for G49;
- bit 4: W1 sharing, reserved for G58;
- bit 5: verify (this item);
- bit 6: no reserve (this item, experimental).
Bits 5 and 6 do nothing without bit 1.

Plumbing:
- the miniport reads the value at boot: VcrDiagGet(L"D3DFastSetup", 0) in VcrFindAdapter;
- it travels in a vcr_info word appended at the end, because vcr_info.flags has no room for multi-bit switches;
- VcrDd2dInit zeroes info before the IOCTL, so an older miniport arms nothing, and masks the value to the bits this build implements.
It is chip-generic, so the 86Box Voodoo3 bed can exercise it first, but it is proven on .124 only.

With the switch off, every 3D room check runs VcrDdRoom's exact loop (counted), and every vertex is one check followed by its 9/12/15 writes in today's order. The bus traffic, reads and writes alike, is byte for byte as today, and tests pin it.

It is NOT safe to land default-on. It changes bus timing and how long it takes to notice a hung engine, and the read cost it saves has never been measured. Arming it needs one supervised clean boot per Diag change: boot B (0x22, verify), then boot C (0x02), then optionally boot D (0x42).

Graduation to default-on, in its own commit with the test flipped, requires all of:
- d3dprobe perf --mode setup at --tex 1 at least 10% faster;
- UT2003 flyby DrawPrimitive ms per frame at most 0.95x the baseline;
- render matrix and fifogrid pixel-identical between boots;
- 0 credit misses in the verify boot;
- no 513 a=9 give-up in any boot.

Remove the value with reg delete /v, never REGDELETE.

G48.regression_test:
New tests/native/test_vcr_kmd_fifocredit.c, a true-source test that compiles include/vcr_fifocredit.h.

The model FIFO has 31 entries and a low-water mark of 10. The chip drains d entries per CPU write. The model counts reads, zone_writes (writes that arrive with fewer than LWM empty entries, which the real chip would retry) and overflow. Two transports drive 1000 triangles of 27, 36 and 45 entries:
- old: VcrDdRoom(n) followed by n writes, per vertex;
- new: the header's per-write charge/refill.

Cases (asserting both the old value and the fixed one):
- with instant drain, the old transport reads 3000 times;
- with instant drain, the new transport reads 1286 / 1715 / 2143 times (ceil(N/21)), with zone_writes and overflow both 0;
- with reserve 0, it reads 871 / 1162 / 1452 times;
- with a slow chip (d = 1/4), the new transport has zone_writes 0 and waits > 0, while the old one has zone_writes > 0 (today's exposure, pinned);
- a stalled chip makes the new transport give up after exactly spin_cap reads, with writes at most (free - reserve);
- drop forces the next take to read;
- a reserve of 31 is cut so takes of 15 and of 1 still succeed, where the old-buggy shape would spin forever;
- verify flags injected foreign entries and reports 0 misses without them;
- refill with n = 0 re-bases the credit.

tests/python/test_vcr_kmd_d3d.py adds:
- test_fifo_credit_is_a_default_off_switch:
  - VcrDiagGet(L"D3DFastSetup", 0) is read in VcrFindAdapter;
