G57.gating:
Diag\D3DGuardBand is a REG_DWORD under HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\vcrmp\Diag. It is read at BOOT, like D3D32 and D3DBigTex, because the desktop PDEV and a fullscreen PDEV must report the same caps. VSA-100 only; a Banshee/Voodoo3 logs "ignored". Absent or 0 is OFF.

Bits:
- bit 0 = ON (caps -200/-200/2048/1536, viewport scissor, clip1 + renderMode[21]);
- bit 1 = experiment: renderMode[21] left clear;
- bit 2 = experiment: wide band -1024/-1024/2048/2048;
- bit 3 = OBSERVE: log-only viewport bookkeeping and counters, no caps or register change, usable alone.
Useful values: 8, 9, 1, 11, 13.

Transport: the miniport reads VcrDiagGet(L"D3DGuardBand", 0) and passes it as a field appended to vcr_info (d3d_gb), following G46's convention because flag 0x8000 is over-claimed. The DLL reads it only when info.size covers the field. When armed, event 513 logs "armed".

When off, the proven path is byte-for-byte unchanged: caps, the target sequence's renderMode and clip values, no clip1 write, the same VIEWPORTINFO step, the same Clear bytes. Native tests pin it.

NOT safe to land default-on: it changes what the runtime sends (unclipped geometry, possibly a different DP2 shape), and it moves viewport clipping from the runtime into the HAL. The vendor's PRS 12728 (H&D black intro) shows the failure mode.

Arm with REGWRITE ... D3DGuardBand REG_DWORD <v>, read it back, run the activation check, then safe-reboot.py. One Diag change per clean boot. To disarm, write 0 and reboot (REGDELETE removes keys, not values).

Default-on only after a supervised armed boot where ALL of these hold:
- every gb* d3dprobe test passes at 16 and 32 bpp, windowed and fullscreen;
- the default d3dprobe matrix is unchanged;
- no title on the list regresses in fullscreen screenshots (H&D intro not black, Jedi Knight/MotS view not spilling);
- the gain is measured beyond noise (3 runs each, non-overlapping ranges).
If the gate in the on-box plan fails (TRIANGLEFAN_IMM below 5% of HAL triangles, or a title drawing outside its viewport today), it stays off and drops to P3.

