G61.gating:
New switch Diag\DdBltCaps: a DWORD; absent = 0 = today's caps and today's Dd_Blt body, byte for byte (counter increments only).

The miniport reads it at every IOCTL_VCR_INFO, as it does Accel2DText and DdHeapFloor, so the next mode change picks it up with no reboot. It travels to the display driver in an appended vcr_info.dd_blt_caps field: the flag bits are contested by other designs. VcrDd2dInit zeroes info first, so an older miniport gives 0.

Bits:
- 0x1: source colour key;
- 0x2: depth fill;
- 0x4: stretch;
- 0x8: contract (the already-claimed copy/fill/clipped classes never decline). Implied by any of 0x1-0x4;
- 0x80: FORCECPU, lab only. Every blit of the new path goes to the CPU; never armed for games.

Caps are added only when the 2D engine is usable at DrvGetDirectDrawInfo time. The switch is chip-independent, so the 86Box Voodoo3 bed exercises it.

Default OFF until one supervised clean boot proves it on .124 (one Diag change per boot: absent, then 0x7, then optionally 0x8F). After that the default moves to 0xF through a MOVED_DIAG entry with the evidence path.

Step 0 (counters and logs) is log-only, writes no registers, and lands default-on.

This item is NOT a pure correctness fix that can land default-on. It changes what the runtime routes to the driver, and it adds a new engine command (stretch) that has never run on silicon.

