VERDICT. The gap is real, with the correction the gap itself states. In-game frames on vcr-kmd exist for JK, MotS and Thief II (09-28, b63ea6a5, before the 11-08 fixes) and for UT2004, UT2003 and Halo's timedemo cutscenes (11-12, 95678704). Three things are true of all of them: none was compared with a reference renderer, none has a census, and none is known to come from a Glide-free boot. This is an EVIDENCE gap, not a HAL defect. G73 changes no driver behaviour, no caps, and no proven path. It delivers four things: a repeatable, instrumented, supervised in-game sweep ("the G73 sweep") driven by a versioned scene book; a host census tool; a d3dprobe calibration test; and the evidence and measured compat rows. Eighteen sibling designs (G04, G06, G18, G20, G23, G29, G31, G42, G44, G45, G52, G55, G59, G61, G64, G65, G66, G69) already name this sweep as their in-game check, so it must be a reusable vehicle with fixed scenes and capture points.

NEW FACTS FROM THIS READING.
(a) None of the four 11-12 in-game rings has a census. Each has 1024 entries, 1020 of them DEBUG, with 0 combine lines and 0 ContextCreate lines (first seq vs next_seq: 206545/207568, 96359/97382, 322630/323653, 305093/306116). The only per-title op census on record is still UT2003's MENU (26 set-ups).
