G76.approach:
The gap is real and both halves are measured on the 11-12 rings.

**The ring wraps.** At the deployed LogLevel 3 the 1024-entry ring held the last 17.4 s of UT2004, 62.9 s of UT2003 and 0.5 s of Halo. 1008-1013 of each title's last 1024 entries are DEBUG CreateSurfaceEx destroy notices (513/3). The UT2004 window fetched after the game starts at seq 96,359 against a pre-launch mark of 30,121, so at least 66,237 entries were never seen.

**No counters.** ctx_free logs one line (513/2: DP2 calls, triangles, clears, unparsed opcodes, flushes). Nothing records whether a title sends ZBIAS, flat shading, lines, state blocks, DX5 texture states or unmapped ops. Twenty sibling designs (G08, G09, G13-G16, G22-G33, G35-G37, G40, G42, G52, G02 and more) carry their own step-0 counter slices and wait on G76 for a common home.

The design has three parts. All are log-only, and none writes a register or changes a cap, a DDI answer or the DP2 walk's byte consumption.

**(A) The usage block.**
- New Win32-free, integer-only header `include/vcr_d3duse.h` (the DLL is -mgeneral-regs-only except vcrdd_3d.c, so FOGEND is compared as an IEEE bit pattern).
- Two append-only X-macro tables in the vcr_events.h pattern, each row naming its gap:
  - 70 slots (CNT/MASK/MAX/FIRST/SNAP), including:
    - draw health: dp2_nodraw, nodraw_why, tris_lost, tris_badidx;
    - binds/refusals and render targets: rt_tex, rt_misses, rt_refusals;
    - lines_seen, points_seen, imm_lines, prim_ops (G16's names);
    - STATESET by dwOperation (G40's six kinds plus the first record);
    - skipped opcodes (palette, SETTEXLOD, WINFO, viewport, T&L, EXT) and a DP2 opcode bitmap;
    - drawn-with op/argument masks per stage, tss_dropped, validate calls, combo_unlog;
    - G08's legacy fields verbatim (lgc_v3/17/18/21/44/45 value masks, token counts, lgc_tss12, lgc_misc, lgc_hctx, lgc_dp2fl), legacy_binds;
    - changed-state bitmaps;
    - handle-table live/peak/full.
  - 33 conditions, each counted in triangles drawn while it held: zbias, usew, stencil, ckey, ckey_tex, spec, flat, fill, fogt, fogt_z, fogv, fogv_lost, mip_lin, lodbias, mirror, border, op2x, op_other, argmod, tf_s0, tf_tmu, s1_lost, dither32, bl_dalpha, bl_color1, projected, leg_blend, leg_filt, leg_addr, cylwrap, tex0_ref, tex1_ref, tex_nocrd.
- Conditions are attributed per state epoch, never per triangle:
  - in prepare(), after the texcoord and fog decisions (vcrdd_d3d.c:1338-1360) and before VcrDd3dTarget/State (:1361), vcr_use_epoch adds c->tris minus epoch_tris to the old mask's bits and computes the new mask from c->rs/c->tss/c->tss1 and the walk;
  - ctx_free flushes the open epoch;
  - the drawn-triangle path gets no added instruction.
- Hooks are one-liners in set_rs, the TSS walk, walk(), tri()/imm_tri() (index test still before prepare), compute_regs, log_combo, SETRENDERTARGET, CLEAR/Clear2, TEXBLT, D3d_DrawPrimitives2, ValidateTextureStageState (answer unchanged) and handle_set/forget.
- An explicit STATESET case consumes the same n×12 bytes rec_size did.
- At ctx_free, after the byte-identical 513/2 line, about 36 INFO records go out under a new event VCR_EV_DD_D3DUSE (next free 5xx; 517 provisional, because 514-516 and the 513 sub-codes 24-29 are contested):
  - a = ctx<<16 | record (0 head, k slot triples, 0x100+j condition triples), b/c/d = values, names from the table (≤79 characters);
  - an idle context logs only its head;
  - one WARN line appears when tris_lost or dp2_nodraw > 0 (G02's 'told DD_OK but drew nothing').
- The emitter never dereferences c->pd (G43).

**(B) Ring discipline and tooling.**
- Campaign logging values, read at boot by code that already exists: Diag\LogLevel=2 and Diag\LogEntries=8192 (1 MB non-paged, the same as G04's boots; 16384 allowed). A failed allocation leaves no ring, and the first check after boot catches that.
- deploy_box.py:280 stops forcing LogLevel 3: it writes the value only when absent or with --loglevel.
- New tools/ringwin.py:
  - mark() takes log_next_seq from vcrctl info before the launch;
  - fetch() refuses while the title runs, then EXECs `vcrctl log <mark> > file` and DOWNLOADs it;
  - window_report() names a wrap (`wrapped`, `lost`) and the level in effect.
- New tools/d3duse.py: decode, d3dprobe verdict, a title × gap exposure report built from the rows' gap ids (replacing hal.md §11's inferred table), and a --combos self-check against log_combo.
- --ring in d3dprobe_run.py (shared with G52) and in lan_sweep.py/lan_check.py, so every title's window is saved beside its frames.
- vcrlog.py fetch --via-file.
- After a freeze with the box alive: close the game, then fetch from the mark.

**(C) Optional, with or after G52 (its sampler and LogGate).**
- Sample the creation-path DEBUG floods per process (513/3, 511/7, 513/10), and log the first 32 texture placements (513/11/19/20) per process at INFO, so hal.md's 'read 513/19 at LogLevel 2' becomes possible.
- One INFO summary per process at DestroyDDLocal, which the 11-12 rings show runs in the game's process (pid 480).
- A default-level ring then keeps a whole session.

Old path: the register traffic, caps, answers and walk are byte for byte unchanged; only the ring gains lines.

Not a fix for any title by itself. It is the measurement every P0/P1 D3D decision on .124 waits on, and the ring G04's Max Payne investigation needs.

G76.d3dprobe_test:
**Name:** `usage`. It is explicit (--tests usage), never in the default list, so the 40/40 matrix is unchanged.

**How it works.** It is host-verified: the probe draws a known mix in one device/context, writes "usage_expect" and "pid" into its RESULT, and d3dprobe_run.py --ring reads that context's D3DUSE block from the ring window after the probe exits (the block is written at device release).

**Set-up.** A 64x64 R5G6B5 2-level texture T. All quads lie inside [16,W-16) so the runtime never clips them into fans. The state returns to the probe's baseline (LIGHTING off, CULL NONE, ZENABLE FALSE, DITHER off; d3dprobe.c:1492-1495) after each item. Each item draws 2 triangles.

**Exact checks:**
- zbias (ZBIAS 1) = 2; flat (SHADEMODE FLAT) = 2; spec (SPECULARENABLE with a specular FVF) = 2;
- fogt_z (LINEAR fog, START 0, END 1.0) = 2 and fogt += 2; W-range fog (10..100) adds fogt only; fogv / fogv_lost (FOGTABLEMODE NONE with/without specular) = 2 each;
- mip_lin (MIPFILTER LINEAR) = 2; lodbias (-1.0) = 2; mirror and border = 2 each;
- op2x (MODULATE2X) = 2, with s0_cops bit 5 set; op_other (SUBTRACT) = 2; argmod (TEXTURE|COMPLEMENT) = 2; tf_s0 (MODULATE(TEXTURE, TFACTOR)) = 2;
- s1_lost (stage 1 MODULATE with no stage-0 texture) = 2;
- dither32 = 2 at 32 bpp and 0 at 16 bpp;
- bl_dalpha (SRCBLEND DESTALPHA) = 2; bl_color1 (SRCBLEND SRCCOLOR) = 2;
- lines_seen = 8 (LINELIST 5 + LINESTRIP 3); points_seen = 7;
- 513/2 triangles = the sum issued; tris_lost = tris_badidx = dp2_nodraw = 0.

**Observed, recorded as runtime facts, not gating:**
- usew, stencil without stencil caps, fill (WIREFRAME: fill = 2 or the runtime made lines), projected;
- a state block (CreateStateBlock + ApplyStateBlock): expected ss_* = 0, because D3D8 emulates state blocks for this DDI. A non-zero count makes G40 real for D3D8 titles;
- ValidateDevice → validate ≥ 1 if forwarded.

**Negative controls stay 0:** ckey*, leg_*, lgc_n*, legacy_binds (D3D8 cannot send them; G75's d3d7probe covers them), tex*_ref.

**Pass criterion:**
- every exact row equals the probe's own count, and every control is 0;
- the head's nslots/nconds equal the host's parsed table;
- two consecutive runs give identical blocks (zeroed per context).
Reference old value: on build 95678704 the window has no D3DUSE block, so the verdict is 'absent: a build before G76' = FAIL.

**Where it runs:** --full 640x480x16 and --full 1024x768x32, first on the 86Box Voodoo3 bed.

