G79.approach:
Real and fixable, and entirely tooling: no vcrdd, vcrmp or vcrprobe byte changes in phases A-C. Existing records show the back-buffer mechanism the gap called "inferred":
- The GDI surface is the primary at vcr_desktop_offset() (vcrmp_hw.c:700-708, vcrmp.c:706).
- A D3D chain's second buffer comes from the DirectDraw heap: on 11-12 the ring shows "primary at 3d00000" and "ContextCreate 1: target 300000".
- On 10-04 Max Payne's scan-out start read 004b0000 while its GDI surface sat at 03b50000, so a GDI capture at that moment read the back buffer.
- At UT2003's 116.7 of 123 ms in DrawPrimitive, about half of all GDI frames are a back buffer mid-render (inferred). That puts today's in-game "white terrain / striped band" frames in doubt.

Phase A, capture (tools/vcrctl.c plus include/vcr_fbshot.h; user mode, escape-free, no DC):
- `scanout [--watch MS] [--pid PID]` (registers only):
  - layer and start register;
  - gdi_offset, from the miniport's own vcr_desktop_offset (link common/vcr_modes.c) or Diag\DesktopOffset;
  - front_is_gdi;
  - a ~1 kHz start-register watch (timeBeginPeriod(1), TIME_CRITICAL), giving flips/s, distinct buffers, max_gap and a lower_bound flag;
  - with --pid, the game's priority class and CPU share; the foreground pid checked before and after.
- `fbshot --probe` flags (all optional):
  - `--lines N`: every Nth screen line plus h-1, full width; about 1/4 of the 1.4 s full read at N=4, with no kernel change;
  - `--burst K --gap MS`;
  - `--prio critical`: HIGH class plus TIME_CRITICAL only around each frame's read loop, never REALTIME, capped by `--cap-ms` 3000;
  - per-frame telemetry: wall_ms, cpu_ms from GetThreadTimes, ioctl_us_avg/max, flip_rows. cpu ≈ wall means bus-bound; cpu ≪ wall means starved.
- A new vcr_fb_recheck_cross keeps the SLI/AA gate re-read every 64 screen lines for sparse line sets. The old y%64 rule would leave 192-line holes at N=3.
- A pure vcr_ctl_needs_dc table. esc() consults an escape guard whose signal is G04's Diag\Live\D3DBeat.
- With no new flag, fbshot behaves as today: the same reads, BMP and JSON keys, with telemetry keys appended.

Phase B: KMD/tools/frame_verdict.py (the module G44 and G73 expect; Pillow only). Classes:
- blank: one 15-bit colour ≥ 98 %, or sd < 3;
- garbage: ≥ 50 % of 16x16 tiles have > 40 % saturated pixels and hue entropy > 2.6 bits;
- stale, exact: the pre-launch desktop's bytes reinterpreted at the new mode's GDI offset, ≥ 50 % of bright predicted pixels within ±8;
- stale, heuristic: horizontal lag-1/lag-2 ratio ≥ 3 and lag-1 ≥ 8 levels;
- sparse: dominant colour ≥ 85 %;
- content: anything else.

Validation on 257 committed .124 frames:
- garbage: exactly the two 09-28 H&D noise frames the sweep passed (tiles 0.68; the best content frame scores 0.048);
- stale: nine frames (AvP ×5, UT2004 30 s on 09-29, the 11-12 045 s frame, and UT 436 30/60 s, which are a Glide title's GDI frames);
- 256 of 257 frames get the same class on an every-4th-line thumbnail;
- the exact predictor matches 70.3 % on the 11-12 UT2004 045 s frame and 0.0-0.1 % on in-game frames, and the true offset beats shifted ones.

The module also hosts G06's confetti and G44's grass metrics verbatim, an edge check (flags all four pre-fix V-01 frames and no post-fix frame), a contact sheet and the presentmark decoder.

Phase C, verdicts:
- A sample = a watch, one GDI shot (tagged gdi or gdi-front) and a 3-frame probe burst 1 s apart. Overlay-layer GDI frames are ignored. The best frame wins, in source order engine > probe > gdi-front > gdi.
- Title picture and verdict:
  - garbage in ≥ 2 samples → FAIL;
  - stale in every sample, with the front confirmed → FAIL;
  - content in a recipe's in-game window plus its marker → PASS (in-game, front buffer or GDI only);
  - any other content → PASS (menu only);
  - otherwise → CHECK "no informative frame".
- Notes: "stopped presenting" and "edge unrendered".
- The sweep writes compat `runs`, never `verified`.
- Three recipes proven on .124 on 11-12 move into lan_check: the UT2004 spectator botmatch, the UT2003 flyby and Halo -timedemo. The UE2 marker is `Bringing Level (?!Entry\.)\S+ up for play`.
- lan_check's `stddev < 4` rule becomes blank/garbage/stale; lan_sweep keeps starts_verdict for comparison; lanparty adopts the probe last.

Phase D (conditional on bus-bound telemetry): a vcrprobe gather IOCTL, additive, no reboot.

d3dprobe `presentmark` proves the tooling on silicon. Priority P1.

